% shatter - soak it, freeze it, and break it if freezing is not enough
%
% The recipe: ?e carries wet, someone else lands chilled on it (the level's
% physics turns that into frozen). Where frozen stops ?e, that is the end -
% stalling is a finisher. Otherwise the blow its weakness names shatters it.

% === Methods ===

% Frozen is enough.
shatter(?e) :-
    if(stops(?e, frozen), receptive(?e, chilled), supplier(?p, wet, ?e)),
    do(supply(?p, wet, ?e), inflict(chilled, ?e, ?p), confirmStopped(?e)).

% Frozen, then broken: the blow its weakness names (a stunning blow on
% something frozen shatters it), from anyone.
shatter(?e) :-
    if(not(stops(?e, frozen)), weakness(?e, ?in, frozen, ?out), stops(?e, ?out),
       receptive(?e, frozen), receptive(?e, chilled), receptive(?e, ?in), supplier(?p, wet, ?e)),
    do(supply(?p, wet, ?e), inflict(chilled, ?e, ?p), ensureFrozen(?e), deliver(?in, ?e, none),
       confirmStopped(?e)).
ensureFrozen(?e) :- if(tag(?e, frozen)), do().
